%N A398992 The binomial matrix of the central binomial numbers. Square array read by ascending antidiagonals.
%C A398992 See the comments and links in A399000.
%H A398992 Peter Luschny, <a href="https://github.com/PeterLuschny/Gists/blob/main/GnomonicExpansionAndBinomialMatrices.ipynb">Gnomonic Expansion and Binomial Matrices</a>, a Python notebook.
%F A398992 A(n, n) = CB(n) := binomial(2*n, n).
%F A398992 A(n, k) = Sum_{m=0..d} binomial(d, m) * s^(d - m) * CB(p + m), where d = abs(n - k), p = min(n, k), s = 1 if k <= n, otherwise -1.
